  "exact_claim": "For seven original X-COP gas/star/hydro profiles, treating declared quoted errors as deterministic knot boxes and using fixed log-log mass interpolation, every one of 189 gas intervals intersecting 100\u20131000 kpc has s_min>1 (minimum 1.0847944099720517). All 252 original shells and 2268 interval-midpoint force/branch evaluations have Delta_min>0 (minimum 1.6206692315737158e-11 m/s\u00b2), across Q/R/registered M, both a0 values and distinct vacuum/H histories. Thus all 84 cluster-branch combinations retain the specified conventional-inertia, steady source-free spherical flow sign contradiction with outward-decreasing extra scalar pressure. This is conditional deterministic robustness, not observational significance. A644 full-support hydro monotonicity is infeasible and is not used as a vacuous premise; all 21 profile boxes are monotone feasible on the knots required for 100\u20131000 kpc.",
  "new_assumptions": [
    "Knot-mass intervals are constructed before log-log interpolation; this is the explicit family being bounded, distinct from separately interpolating central/error curves.",
    "Gas-error inflation factors are supplemental deterministic sensitivity parameters, not enlarged observational confidence regions."
  ],
